                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00001                             nam       GShell              Graphics Shell
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00002                             ttl       Source derived by Kent D. Meyers.
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00003         
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00004         * Signal handlers will have to handle new RBF call for directory updates
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00005         * DIR has to be open (uses path #), but can be in READ+DIR mode
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00006         *  Renames, etc. will have to close DIR 1st, do function, re-open.
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00007         
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00008         * Compressed Version. Started February 7, 1988. Completed February 29.
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00009         * Upgraded Version. Started March 2, 1988. Finished by KDM Feb 13, 1994
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00010         * NITROS9 ONLY VERSION. Started August 8,1998 by LCB
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00011         * NOTE: When GSHPAL added, got rid of DEVICSET, and 2 other SETS from env.file
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00012         *       check in DP (3 DP bytes back)
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00013         * NOTE: HAVE TRIED 5 ROWS OF ICONS (ICONYMAX=143, ICONROWH=32, ICONSCR=20), &
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00014         *       IT FITS, BUT LOOKS REALLY CROWDED. IF WE MAKE THE NEW "SYSTEM" 6 PIXEL
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00015         *       WIDE FONT ALSO SHORTER (LIKE FONT #$27, WHICH IS THE 8 PIXEL WIDE VERSION)
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00016         *       IT MIGHT WORK THEN.
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00017         * Killed all calls to F.SLEEP, embedded (shorter & faster)
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00018         * Should do F$CpyMem of <$40-43 in direct page to get real RAM size - both
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00019         *   6809 and NitrOS9. Then we can eliminate RAM= from the Env.fil entirely!
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00020         
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00021         * NOTE (6309 ONLY): ALL STD -2,S TO CHECK THE D FLAG CAN BE CHANGED TO TSTD
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00022         *(SAME SIZE, FASTER)
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00023         
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00024         * EOS (Ease of Use) modifications:
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00025         * LCB- 12/15/2017 - New printer and trash can icons from Nick Marentes (and trash can position)
                      (s_6809/gshell.asm):00026         *
